# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq API key for the portfolio chatbot.
#
# 1. Copy this file next to itself and drop the ".example":
#
#        secrets/groq_api_key.txt
#
# 2. Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys - it starts with "gsk_".
# 3. Replace the placeholder line at the bottom with your key.
# 4. Point GROQ_API_KEY_FILE at your copy:
#
#        # Windows PowerShell
#        $env:GROQ_API_KEY_FILE = "D:\path\to\secrets\groq_api_key.txt"
#
#        # macOS / Linux
#        export GROQ_API_KEY_FILE=/path/to/secrets/groq_api_key.txt
#
#    then run the app:  streamlit run ui/app.py
#
# The key is yours, it is read at startup, and this directory is gitignored
# (apart from this .example), so a filled-in copy cannot be committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY A FILE RATHER THAN A VARIABLE
#
# A key you export lands in your shell history and in the environment of every
# process that shell launches. A key in a file does neither. It also survives
# closing the terminal, which an export does not.
#
# The simpler routes still work and are fine for local use:
#
#     .streamlit/secrets.toml     GROQ_API_KEY = "gsk_..."     (the app)
#     .env                        GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...         (the CLI scripts)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT
#
# Comment lines (starting with #) and blank lines are ignored, so you can leave
# all of this in place. Any of these work for the key itself:
#
#     gsk_your_key_here
#     GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_key_here
#     GROQ_API_KEY="gsk_your_key_here"
#
# Trailing newlines, Windows line endings, surrounding quotes and a Notepad
# byte-order mark are all handled. You do not need to be careful with this file.
#
# Leaving the placeholder below unedited counts as NO key: you get the app's
# "not configured" page rather than a 401 claiming your key is invalid.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_replace_this_with_your_own_key
